 "memo": "Read all 47 cells in full before grouping, then grouped within each cell by the action the policy asks for (or, for background cells, the claim it makes about AI). I kept a running label list and reused labels across cells where the idea matched (e.g. 'Citing and disclosing AI use', 'Verifying AI output', 'Using approved AI tools', 'Submitting AI work as one's own', 'Fabrication and deception with AI', 'Human review of AI grading', 'Instructors learning about AI'). Hard calls: in the large instructor before-course cell I split assignment redesign (19 policies) from goal-based decisions, equity/access, peer alignment and misuse planning, and placed P99.03 (design to reduce temptation) with misuse prevention rather than redesign; in student course permit I separated broad blanket permission from conditional 'within stated limits' permission; feedback-on-own-work uses (P129.x, P93.08) were folded into 'AI as a study aid' to stay within 7 groups; several singletons were kept only where clearly distinct (e.g. P62.23 research ethics, P126.04 security, P31.05 instructor verification with 44 universities, P101.02 opt-out of AI grading). Groups are ordered by summed university counts; PIDs within groups are ordered by count."
}